    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "I added the grace period, and `bin/e2e` passes: the test-data replay is clean and the acceptance test succeeds. An invoice now only becomes Overdue once today is more than 7 days past its due date.\n\n- **The rule:** it lives in one place, `Invoice.statusWhenPaid` in `src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/invoices/Invoice.java`. A new `GRACE_DAYS = 7` constant sets the length. An invoice is overdue when something is still due and today is after the due date plus 7 days.\n- **Client list:** the overdue amount there adds up invoices whose status is `OVERDUE`, using that same method. So it follows the new rule without its own change.\n- **Comments:** I updated the description of overdue in `InvoiceStatus.java` and the front end's `invoice.service.ts` to mention the grace period.\n\n**Decision for you:** \"Paid late\" still means the payment came after the due date, with no grace period. The request only covered Overdue, so I left this alone. If a payment made within the week shouldn't count as late, it's a one-line change in the same method; say if you want it.",
